    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. There are only three test files (`AcceptanceTest` plus its `AcceptanceBase` and `AuditLogCapture` support classes), and the one test passed.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` \u2014 the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans \u2014 while keeping `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field.\n\n2. **`CountryDialingCodes.java` (new)** \u2014 Extracted the recognised country-code knowledge (`{61\u21929, 1\u219210}`) and the longest-prefix `matching(...)` / `nationalLength(...)` lookups into a single shared source of truth, since both normalization and display formatting need it.\n\n3. **`TelephoneNormalizer.java`** \u2014 Refactored to delegate to `CountryDialingCodes` instead of holding its own copy of the country-code map and detection logic (no behavior change, no duplication).\n\n4. **`TelephoneFormatter.java` (new)** \u2014 Single-responsibility formatter that turns a stored E.164 value into display form: recognised country code, a space, then national digits grouped in threes (`+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`), with a sensible best-effort fallback for unrecognised codes.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Wired the derived field in via a `telephoneDisplay(owner)` default method invoked from a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression, mirroring the existing `displayName` pattern.\n\nThe formatting logic lives in its own util, the country-code knowledge is shared rather than copied, and the model/DTO wiring follows the conventions already in the codebase.",
